     "explanation": "A free fall was far too fast to time in the 1600s, when there were no stopwatches. Rolling a ball down a shallow incline is essentially a fall stretched out over more time, keeping the same underlying rule of motion while letting Galileo mark and measure each stage. It was a brilliant way to make a fast process visible.",
